From: PowOS <mats@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: restore existing tasks on show and reconnect

Reopening an already foreground Android task need not produce a new focus
event. Restore its minimized Linux window explicitly on show. When its
consumer reconnects, restore focus after watchWindow has marked it visible
again; the first-export-only focus call misses subsequent connections.

--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
@@ -295,7 +295,6 @@
             m_window->setDesktops({desktop});
         }
         m_exported = true;
-        focus();
     }
     // A full-screen window keeps the size it has now through output changes (a game started unfolded keeps
     // rendering 2268x2440 on the cover screen) - the task scales it instead (viewport()).
@@ -303,6 +302,7 @@
         m_window->setProperty("powosKeepFullScreenGeometry", true); // Window::checkWorkspacePosition
     }
     watchWindow(m_window);
+    focus();
     attach(m_window);
     // Menus, popups and dialogs it opens from now on are drawn into the task too (dialogs over it, where KWin placed
     // them - centred on it), and moved with it: they live with it on the tasks desktop.
@@ -1280,6 +1280,7 @@
         return false;
     }
     if (AnlandWindowTask *task = taskFor(window)) {
+        task->focus();
         // Already a task: to the front - as what it is: a game's own full-screen task stays full screen (the drawer's
         // launch of a game that KWin already showed full screen made it a floating task, the game scaled into it).
         QStringList open{QStringLiteral("open"), QString::number(task->id()), window->desktopFileName(), window->caption()};
